# Where saved shots + their edit metadata live on disk. On the VPS this is
# set by docker-compose.yml to a mounted volume so photos survive rebuilds;
# defaults to ./.data/photos for local dev.
#
# Note: this only persists when the app itself runs somewhere with a real
# writable disk (i.e. Docker on the VPS). A Vercel deployment's serverless
# functions have an ephemeral filesystem — saving a photo there will not
# reliably survive between requests. See README.md.
PHOTOS_DIR=

# On Vercel, storage switches automatically to Vercel Blob instead of
# PHOTOS_DIR the moment this is set — no other config needed. It is NOT
# something you type in by hand: in the Vercel dashboard, go to your
# project's Storage tab -> Create Database -> Blob, connect it to this
# project, and Vercel injects this env var itself. Redeploy afterwards so
# the new function picks it up. Leave unset for the VPS/Docker or local-dev
# path above.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
